1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,848
Every team at this hackathon has to submit a

2
00:00:03,848 --> 00:00:07,396
demo video. Most of us are making it right

3
00:00:07,396 --> 00:00:08,973
now, at 3 a.m.

4
00:00:08,973 --> 00:00:11,338
A good one needs a script,

5
00:00:11,338 --> 00:00:12,915
a clean recording, editing,

6
00:00:12,915 --> 00:00:14,492
a voiceover and captions.

7
00:00:14,492 --> 00:00:16,463
That's hours you don't have.

8
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,301
Pit Crew makes the pitch video for you.

9
00:00:20,301 --> 00:00:21,702
Paste your live link,

10
00:00:21,702 --> 00:00:23,452
or just your GitHub repo.

11
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:25,977
Here's a real run.

12
00:00:25,977 --> 00:00:27,454
I paste Excalidraw's link,

13
00:00:27,454 --> 00:00:31,147
pick a narrator, and ask to review the script first.

14
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,072
An agent on HarnessRouter explores the site and plans

15
00:00:35,072 --> 00:00:38,596
the pitch, while our server records each step in Chromium.

16
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,468
Before anything is voiced,

17
00:00:40,468 --> 00:00:42,805
I get the outline and a pitch check,

18
00:00:42,805 --> 00:00:44,557
and I can change any line.

19
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:48,801
Then it's voiced and rendered into a finished 1080p

20
00:00:48,801 --> 00:00:50,746
pitch video, ready to download.

21
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,703
No live link? OmniSTEM is just a GitHub repo.

22
00:01:00,703 --> 00:01:03,906
Pit Crew ran it inside a HarnessRouter sandbox and

23
00:01:03,906 --> 00:01:04,973
recorded it there.

24
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,273
DevPad's API ran the same way,

25
00:01:10,273 --> 00:01:13,276
and its video shows the real responses,

26
00:01:13,276 --> 00:01:14,563
sign-in errors included.

27
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,836
And Hunt the Wumpus,

28
00:01:18,836 --> 00:01:22,293
a Unity game, got its video from the team's

29
00:01:22,293 --> 00:01:26,517
own gameplay clip, narrated from frames the agent actually looked at.

30
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,015
Here's how it works.

31
00:01:31,015 --> 00:01:34,875
Our server hands the project to an agent on

32
00:01:34,875 --> 00:01:38,735
HarnessRouter, which explores the site or runs the repo,

33
00:01:38,735 --> 00:01:41,308
and writes the plan as JSON.

34
00:01:41,308 --> 00:01:44,738
Our server checks every statistic against its source,

35
00:01:44,738 --> 00:01:47,740
records the demo, you review the script,

36
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:51,171
then ElevenLabs voices it and Remotion renders it.

37
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,410
Tonight we tested it on Excalidraw,

38
00:01:55,410 --> 00:01:58,086
Hoppscotch, Carbon, Mermaid and Squoosh,

39
00:01:58,086 --> 00:02:01,831
plus three student projects straight from GitHub.

40
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,756
Next: a pitch video for every launch.

41
00:02:05,756 --> 00:02:08,289
Product Hunt, demo days, investor updates.

42
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:12,124
Paste your link, and Pit Crew makes the pitch.
